 ## Project map
 
-- `index.html` — portfolio content and site structure.
+- `index.html` — home introduction and selected project features.
+- `projects.html` — complete live public repository catalogue for GitLab `paysonism` and GitHub `430L`.
+- `music.html` and `music-player.html` — music index and per-track player pages.
+- `business.html` — company overview panels and per-company timelines.
 - `forum.html` — Mercury-themed community forum page.
-- `css/mercury.css` — all visual styling.
+- `css/mercury.css` — all visual styling; new pages reuse the existing Mercury classes and stylesheet.
 - `theme/` and `assets/` — images and existing Y2K UI assets.
 - `js/chat.js` and `js/forum.js` — browser clients.
+- `js/music-data.js` and `js/business-data.js` — editable music and company content records.
+- `js/music.js`, `js/business.js`, and `js/projects.js` — the new page renderers and repository catalogue client.
+- `CONTENT_EXPANSION_PLAN.md` — page map, content model, and visual/functional acceptance checks.
 - `worker/index.js` — production Worker with chat and forum APIs.
 - `db/schema.ts` and `drizzle/` — production database schema and migrations.
 - `scripts/` — cross-platform developer scripts.
 
+## Adding music and company content
+
+Music records are maintained in `js/music-data.js`. The current entries are visibly marked dummy records for verifying the display; replace them with track objects that have a stable `id`, title, and an `audio` URL/path (for example `assets/music/your-track.mp3`). Set `featured: true` to feature a production. Setup objects use `image`, `title`, and optional caption fields; platform records use `name` and `url`. Replace the generated sample photo and the two original test MP3s in `assets/music/` when adding your real work.
+
+Both the music index and dedicated `music-player.html?track=<id>` page include a customizable 10-band graphic EQ. It uses native Web Audio peaking biquads, smooth parameter changes, saved band/preamp settings, preset curves, bypass, and response-measured automatic headroom. Cross-origin audio files must permit CORS for Web Audio processing; local MP3 files work without that extra setup.
+
+Company records are maintained in `js/business-data.js`. The two current sample companies, example dates, ratings, logo assets, URLs, and achievements are fictional placeholders; replace or remove every marked value. Each record can include `id`, `name`, `startYear`, `endYear` or `current: true`, `description`, `logo`, `website`, `score` (0–5), and a `timeline` array of `{ date, title, description }` milestones. Every company renders its own achievements timeline.
+
+The full repository page fetches the public GitLab and GitHub APIs on page load, follows pagination, groups matching repository names, and links to source, ZIP, clone, README, issues, and releases when available. The left-rail source buttons filter the combined catalogue by host. If either public API is unavailable or rate-limited, the page marks the result as partial and keeps direct profile links available.
+
+Site typography retains Verdana/Tahoma for the main descriptions. Titles use a Bank Gothic-first font stack with the web-delivered Michroma fallback; compact technical labels use Rajdhani. Bank Gothic is used when installed locally, since it is not bundled as an unlicensed font file.
+
 ## Production forum configuration
 
 Production uses a Cloudflare Worker with a D1 database binding named `DB`. Apply every migration in `drizzle/` before deploying the Worker.
